Mixed licensing for boring-bits
==============================

This is not a blanket MIT licence for all repository content.

Scope
-----

1. New toolkit code and documentation (.gitignore, README.md, AGENTS.md,
   CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/compatibility.md, requirements-test.txt,
   tests/test_repository.py and the repository-level notices) are available
   under the MIT License below. Upstream quotations and notices retain their
   own terms.
2. skills/project-prd: original contributions are available under MIT below.
   Adapted material retains its upstream MIT terms. Keep all four files
   together when redistributing; the complete upstream notices are in
   skills/project-prd/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and the adaptation map is in
   skills/project-prd/SOURCE-REUSE.md. This scope does not change those files.
3. skills/business-context-map and skills/workflow-or-agent retain
   CC-BY-4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International), attributed to
   Pedro Borrero, borre.ro. They are NOT relicensed under MIT.
   Terms: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
   Retain attribution and the licence reference, and indicate changes.
   See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md for the changes made in this distribution.
4. No licence is granted here over private business facts, third-party
   documents or other material a user supplies while applying a skill.
   Future contributions must state their licensing scope explicitly.

